Verse 1:
[G]Faith of our fathers, [Am]liv[D7]ing [G]still,
[C]In spite of [G]dungeon, [A7]fire and [D]sword;
[G]O how our hearts beat [Am]high [D7]with [G]joy
[C]Whenever we [G]hear that [A7]glo[D7]rious [G]Word!
[C]Faith of our [G]fathers, [D7]holy [G]faith!
[G]We will be [C]true [Em]to [D]thee [D7]till [G]death.

Verse 2:
[G]Our [Am]fathers, chained [D7]in [G]prisons dark,
[C]Were [G]still in [A7]heart and [D]conscience free:
[G]How [Am]sweet would [D7]be their [G]children's fate.
[C]If [G]they, like [A7]them, [D7]could die [G]for thee!
[C]Faith [G]of our [D7]fathers, [G]holy faith!
[G]We [C]will [Em]be true [D]to [D7]thee [G]till death.

Verse 3:
[G]Faith [Am]of our [D7]fathers, we [G]will love
[C]Both friend [G]and foe [A7]in all [D]our strife;
[G]And preach [Am]Thee, too, [D7]as love [G]knows how
[C]By [G]kindly [A7]words [D7]and [G]virtuous life.
[C]Faith [G]of our [D7]fathers, [G]holy faith!
[G]We [C]will [Em]be true [D]to [D7]thee [G]till death.
